  "problem": "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is prime, or $x$ is composite or it is prime.\"",
  "worked_solution": "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is composite or it is prime\" with the phrase \"$x$ is prime or it is composite.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is prime, or $x$ is prime or it is composite.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is prime or $x$ is prime, or it is composite.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is prime or $x$ is prime\" to just \"$x$ is prime.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is prime, or it is composite.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is prime or composite.\"",
